2 CONT Here the family of Antoine DESROSIERS and Anne LENEUF of the HERISSON!
2 CONT
2 CONT DESROSIERS, Antoine (Antoine & Sylvie) , Baptized 1617-04-14 Renaison. (The Loire), France, Deceased 1691-08-08, Buried 1691-08-09 Champlain (Quebec)
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married 1647 Renaison  (The Loire:), France, marriage contract 1647-11-24 (Notary Boujonnier)
2 CONT
2 CONT LENEUF of the HERISSON, Anne (Michel LENEUF &.., according to DGFQ 348, born about 1632 (census-1666, Sép-1702) Caen (Calvados:), France, buried 1702-12-05 Quebec (Quebec)
2 CONT
2 CONT 1) Anne , born 1661-11-12, baptized 1661-11-12 Three-Rivers (Quebec), died 1731-02-23, buried 1731-02-24 Champlain (Quebec), marriage contract 1674-04-04 heading 1674-04-14 (notary Guillaume Larue) Jacques TURCOT , married Champla
2 CONC in (Quebec) 1702-04-24 Jean Baptiste DEBIDABÉ aka TROISVILLE
2 CONT
2 CONT 2) Antoine , born 1664-08-30, baptized 1664-08-30 Three-Rivers (Quebec), deceased between 1737-06-17 and 1742-01 Berthierville (Quebec), married Champlain (Quebec) 1696-11-26 Marie Renee LEPELLÉ
2 CONT
2 CONT 3) Jean , Married Champlain (Quebec) 1682-01-20 Marie Francoise Perrine DANDONNEAU
2 CONT
2 CONT 4) Marie , Baptized 1650-06-16 Three-Rivers (Quebec), Died After 1711-02-18, Married Three-Rivers (Quebec) 1664-02-19 Alexandre RAUX
2 CONT
2 CONT 5) Marie Jeanne , born about 1671 (rec-1681, conf-1681), 1673 (m-1687), deceased after 1744-08-28, married Champlain (Quebec) 1687-03-18 Claude DROUET of RICHARVILLE
2 CONT
2 CONT 6) Michel , marriage contract  under private signature 1679-01-14 (notary Antoine Adhémar) Marie Thomas ARTAULT
2 CONT
2 CONT 7) Pierre , Married Champlain (Quebec) 1693-04-27 Marguerite AUBUCHON
2 CONT
2 CONT Other information on this family
2 CONT
2 CONT Source or reference: Ferdinand Desrosiers; Program research in historical demography of the University of Montreal (Prdh-rab)
2 CONT -------------------------------------------------
2 CONT The following was acquired from <http://ourworld.compuserve.com/homepages/MarjChapman/TRDUHERR.HTM>:
2 CONT
2 CONT MICHEL  LeNEUF du HÉRISSON
2 CONT
2 CONT His only child and daughter, Anne born 1632 in the bourg of Thierry in Caen, Normandy married Antoine DesROSIERS in 1649 is my direct ancestor.
2 CONT
2 CONT Antoine Desrosiers and Anne duHérisson had eight children. Sons Jean born 1657 and Antoine born 1664, were members of an association created in 1683 between nine men from Champlain for the purpose of fur trading. The composition o
2 CONC f these associates is noteworthy in that it concentrated the power of three influential families in the region: Dandonneau (Huguenot fur-trading merchants), Chorel and Aubuchon. Jean's wife was Françoise Dandonneau. The associatio
2 CONC n dissolved after the summer of 1688 when Jacques Babie, merchant and principal investor, died.
2 CONT
2 CONT All the sons were involved in the business of procuring and selling furs. Son, Michel dit Desilets born 1652 married Thomasse Artault the daughter of an Algonquin and a fur trader, son Jean dit LeFrenière married Françoise Dandonn
2 CONC eau as mentioned above, Antoine dit DuTremble was part of the syndicate mentioned above and received a passport in 1689 to trade in the west. The west, in this case, was probably no further than the Great Lakes. To control the fur
2 CONC  trading and collect appropriate taxes, the French government issued passports (permits), a form of license. They were difficult to acquire since in many years, only 25 were issued. To conduct fur trading or to travel west without
2 CONC  a passport was considered illegal and subject to punishment, most often fines or the confiscation of furs.
2 CONT
2 CONT Son, Pierre dit Dargy born around 1667 married Marguerite AUBUCHON whose uncle was active in the trade.
2 CONT
2 CONT Anne LeNeuf duHérisson died in Champlain in October 1711 at the age of 79.
2 CONT ------------------------------------------------
