2 TITL Ancestry Family Trees
1 NOTE Married 19 Feb 1664 Alexander Raoul (Rault) (son of Louis & Jacqueline Robin, bap. 1636, bur. 6 Jul 1692 at Champlain) at Immaculee Conception de Trois- Rivieres, St Maurice, Quebec, Canada; have copy of this record; sources: (c. 
2 CONC 19-01 Ameau); family (10 children) listed in Jette pg 968; a short bio of Antoine Desrosiers acquired from the internet (copy filed 29-2); Tanguay Vol I pg 192; Tanguay Vol I pg 509 shows family with 10 children; <http://membres.l
2 CONC ycos.fr/ancetre/desrosiers.htm< (copy filed 29-2 also in her father's internal textfile); also see the short bio of her spouse printed below.
2 CONT "You Ancient Canadian Family Ties"-Olivier pg 278.
2 CONT Tanguay Vol I pg 192.
2 CONT 1666 census of Trois-Rivieres shows this family as follows: Alexander Raoul, age 30, carpenter; his wife Marie Desroziers, age 15.  Source filed in censuses.
2 CONT "The Grand Families" from the internet (filed 29-2).
2 CONT <http://membres.lycos.fr/ancetre/desrosiers.htm< (copy filed 29-2 also in her father's internal textfile).
2 CONT ------------------------------------------------
2 CONT The following was acquired from <http://membres.lycos.fr/ancetre/RaultA.htm> (copy filed 29-2); a translated version follows:
2 CONT
2 CONT ALEXANDRE   RAULT
2 CONT
2 CONT Son of Louis Raoul, merchant, and Jacquette Robin, the ancestor Alexandre Rault, Rheault or Raoul is baptized December 20 1633, at the parish Notre Dame de Deyrançon, in the former provincemof Aunis, currently the department of De
2 CONC ux-Sevres.
2 CONT
2 CONT On November 12 1661, Alexandre is godfather to Anne Desrosiers, daughter of the ancestor Antoine Desrosiers and Anne LeNeuf duHérisson and sister of her future spouse.
2 CONT
2 CONT In fact, the master carpenter, Alexandre Rault goes on January 19 1664, to the notary Ameau with his young fiancée, Marie Desrosiers, born at Three Rivers, June 16 1650, elder daughter of the family.  The wedding ceremony takes pl
2 CONC ace at the chapel of Three Rivers, February 19 following.
2 CONT
2 CONT On the census of 1666, Alexandre Rault is 30 years old and his spouse is fifteen years old, at Three Rivers.  In 1667, he possesses eight acres in value at the Petit Cap-de-la-Madeleine.  In 1681, the ancestor Alexandre Rault is 5
2 CONC 0 years old and his spouse, Marie Desrosiers is 31 years old, at Champlain.
2 CONT
2 CONT Ten children were born of this couple btween 1669 and 1691.  The oldest was a weaver of the linen just like my mother, Pierrette Boisvert.
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph-François Rault was born about 1669.  He is registered in the census of 1681, being 12 years old.  He marries June 21 1695, two days after the signature of a marriage contract with the notary Normandin.  The happy spouse is 
2 CONC Françoise Dubois,  born March 3 1674, daughter of Rene Dubois, alias Brisebois and Anne-Juilienne Dumont.
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph-François Rault practiced the trapping of furs in the country of the Outaouais.  Eleven children are born in this new generation.  The seventh one of this family, follows the link, in this généalogy.
2 CONT
2 CONT Joseph Rault was born and baptized July 25 1705, at Champlain.  He marie  in 1724 Marie Catherine Lefebvre, then in a second marriage\s, September 12 1740, with Marie Jeanne Leblanc, born April 4 1712, daughter of Rene Leblanc, al
2 CONC ias Labrie, and Jeanne Bourbeau.
2 CONT
2 CONT The fourth generation continues with their daughter Marie-Josèphe Rault, baptized February 16 1745, becomes the spouse February 3 1777, of Pierre Héon, born in 1740, son of the ancestor Charles Héon and Anne Clémenceau-Beaulieu.
2 CONT
2 CONT The ancestor Alexandre Rault dies January 5 1692, at the age about 60 years and is buried under the name of Raux, January 6 1692, at Champlain.
2 CONT
2 CONT His spouse, Marie Desrosiers survives at least about twenty years, after the death of her husband.  She deceases about 1712.
2 CONT ------------------------------------------------ .
