1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Michel Ignace Drouet Sieur de Baudricourt was one of four of my 6th Great Uncles who were captured in the Chickasaw campaign of 1736. Three were captured and killed. They (all) were reportedly, burned at the stake,
2 CONC  while singing psalms. Michel was captured, but managed to escape. The report he later gave, and account of the event was invaluable, at that time. The following members of the Drouet de Richerville family were killed; Etienne Dro
2 CONC uet de Richerville (de Belecart), Louis Drouet De la Graviere and Denis-Didier Drouet de Richerville. All were sons of Claude Drouet de Richerville. Many other Midwest Frenchmen lost their lives, including: Pierre Groston de St. A
2 CONC nge and Francois-Marie Bissot de Vincennes, from whom our hometown (Vincennes, IN) was named. Vincennes is also a blood relative of the Richardvilles. Michel Ignace Drouet de Baudricourt also fought in the Chickasaw capaign of 173
2 CONC 8, as a lieutenant, and had the honor of carrying the French colors. His younger brother Claude Drouet de Carqueville fought along side him, as well. Denis-Didier Drouet de Richerville was the Grandfather of Miami Indian Chief Jea
2 CONC n-Baptiste Richardville..........
