2 CONT Notes from Richard Ball - http://www.ballfamilyrecords.co.uk/bosmandevriesbuys/I135.html According to the inventory drawn up after his death they also had a house in Cape Town (bought from Jan Hop) and another farm in Drakenstein 
2 CONC called 'Lekkerwyn' A letter from the Chamber of Delft, dated 16 December 1688, stated:
2 CONT
2 CONT With this ship we have again permitted the following French Refugees to sail to the Cape and earn their living as freemen, Pierre de Villiers, Abraham de Villiers and Jacob de Villiers, all three brothers born near la Rochelle. We
2 CONC  are informed that these persons have a good knowledge of laying out vineyards and managing the same, and thus we hope that the Company will acquire their good service.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Zion, left Holland on the 8th January, 1689, and arrived on the 6th May following. (C.G.Botha, French Refugees at the Cape, page 89)
2 CONT  Will - Bosman, Hermanus & Elisabeth de Villiers - 1719, Cape Archives, CJ 2599,54
2 CONT
