1 NAME Joseph-Antoine /Richardville/
2 GIVN Joseph-Antoine
2 SURN Richardville
2 _MARNM Drouet de Richerville
1 SEX M
1 BURI
2 PLAC The Old Cathedral French & Indian Cemetery
2 ADDR
3 CITY Vincennes
3 STAE Indiana
3 CTRY United States
1 BIRT
2 DATE 8 JAN 1759
2 ADDR
3 CITY Vincennes
3 STAE Indiana
3 CTRY United States
1 DEAT
2 DATE 1 NOV 1831
2 ADDR
3 CITY Vincennes
3 STAE Indiana
3 CTRY United States
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Joseph-Antoine Drouet de Richerville is yet another Ancestor of mine, who was named Joseph Antoine or Antoine Joseph. This all becomes very confusing. However, it eventually becomes easier, as family distinctions a
2 CONC re made and of course, with very close attention paid to ALL dates. According to my limited research, he apparently was known as Antoine Drouet throughout most of his life. Of course, along with this comes even more confusion. I f
2 CONC ound a court document from the early 1800's, on which he signed his name as Antoine Drouette, which is another variant of the name and spelling of the name. Others include: Drouet, Drouet de Richerville, Richardville and Dericharv
2 CONC ille, just to name a few. I've only found this particular spelling used by Antoine. However, others may have indeed used it, as well. I'm including a link to an article in The Indiana Magazine of History from 1978. This is an exce
2 CONC llent source for early Drouet de Richardville information. It was written by Donald Chaput, who at the time was Senior Curator of history, Los Angeles County Museum of Natural History.
2 CONT
2 CONT https://scholarworks.iu.edu/journals/index.php/imh/article/view/10088/13887
