2 DATE 3 JAN 1833
2 ADDR
3 CITY Dover
3 STAE Newfoundland
3 CTRY Canada
1 OCCU Lieutenant in the British Indian Department, and a United Empire Loyalist
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Will of Fontenay Dequindre dated 6-6-1831=
2 CONT ==Archives of Ontario, GS1 EssexCo. Reel 719, #219 -404-1823-1834 File # 382: 7. JWP==
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Note:''' His daughter,Catherine, widow of Paul Reaume received ? of his personal property.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Full text of the will is as follows:'''
2 CONT
2 CONT In the name of God, I Fontenay Dequindre of the township of Dover in theCounty of Kent in the Western District of Upper Canada being of sounddisposing mind and memory thanks be unto God considering the uncertaintyof this life do m
2 CONC ake, publish and dictate this my last will and testamentin the manner and form following that is today
2 CONT
2 CONT 1. I will that all my just debts and funeral expenses may be paid as soonas conveniently may be.
2 CONT
2 CONT 2. I give, will and devise the north half of Lot 11 in the west side ofthe Belle River in the First Concession of the Township of Maidstone tomy grand daughter Pelagie (JWP Note: m. Narcisse Dauphin) for and duringher life, then t
2 CONC o her children lawfully begotten to share and sharealike, to have and to hold to them, their heirs and assigns forever andin the case the said Pelagie shall die without children lawfully begottenas aforesaid then I give and devise
2 CONC  the said half Lot numbering 11 on theWest Side of Belle River to my grand daughter Nancy (JWP Note: Marie AnneDequindre m. Jean Baptiste Dauphin) Dequindre, sister of said Pelagieduring her life and to her children lawfully begot
2 CONC ten to share and sharealike, to have and to hold to their heirs and assigns forever.
2 CONT
2 CONT 3. I give and bequeath the south half of Lot #11 on the west side ofBelle River in the First Concession of the Township of Maidstone to mygrand daughter Nancy Dequindre (JWP Note: Marie Anne) before mentioned,for and during her li
2 CONC fe then to her children lawfully begotten to shareand share alike, to have and to hold, their heirs and assigns forever andin the event the death of said Nancy (page of folded and illegible)having ? no lawfully begotten children t
2 CONC he said half to Pelagie Dequindresister of the said Nancy Dequindre for and during her life and thereafterto her children lawfully begotten to share and share alike, to have andto hold their heirs and assigns forever.
2 CONT
2 CONT 4. I give and devise to my grand son Charles Dequindre, his heirs andassigns forever, the north half of Lot #11 on the East? Side of BelleRiver, First Concession of Rochester.
2 CONT
2 CONT 5. I give and devise to my friend Charles Reaume his heirs and assignsforever the South Half of Lot # 11 on the East Side of Belle River, FirstConcession of Rochester but should the said Charles die without childrenand before he s
2 CONC hall have attained the age of 21 then I give and devisethe said half lot to his mother, her heirs and assigns forever. (JWPNote: What is the connection to Charles Reaume?)
2 CONT
2 CONT 6. I give and bequeath to my daughter Pelagie, wife of Isaac Dolsen ? ofall my personal property.
2 CONT
2 CONT 7. I give and bequeath to my daughter Catherine, widow of Paul Reaume ?of my personal property.
2 CONT
2 CONT 8. I give and bequeath to my daughter Catherine, wife of Gabriel Peltierof the Township of Dover ? of all my personal property. (JWP Note: Onceagain Fontenay acknowledges Catherine as his daughter but there is noreference to Cathe
2 CONC rine's mother.)
2 CONT
2 CONT 9. I give and bequeath to the children of the late Charles Dequindre (JWPNote: the children of Charles and Sylvie Johnson-Jansen) to be equallydivided among them ? of all my personal property.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source:'''  http://gw.geneanet.org/monartque?lang=fr&p=marie+catherine&n=daigneault+dit+fontenay
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
2 CONT
