1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.familysearch.org/en/tree/person/about/M1L3-6C8
2 CONT Brief Life History of Alexis
2 CONT
2 CONT When Alexis Neveu was born on 14 August 1758, in Île Dupas, D'Autray, Quebec, Canada, his father, Amable Neveu, was 22 and his mother, Marie Anne Lemaitre, was 25. 
2 CONT
2 CONT He married 1st wife MARGUERITE BRULÉ (1765-1807)  on 22 October 1787, in Saint-Cuthbert, Berthier, Quebec, Canada. They were the parents of at least 3 sons and 3 daughters. 
2 CONT Alexis Neveu 1788–1791 (died in infancy)
2 CONT Baby female Neveu 1790–1790 (died in infancy)
2 CONT Joseph Neveu 1792–
2 CONT Marie Marguerite Neveaux 1794–1794 (died in infancy)
2 CONT Antoine Neveu 1795–1795 (died in infancy)
2 CONT Marie Neveu 1800–1833
2 CONT
2 CONT He married 2nd wife Genevieve Morin Chenevert (1781–1851)
2 CONT on 21 septembre 1807 in Saint-Cuthbert, Berthier, Quebec
2 CONT They had at least 10 children
2 CONT Olivier Neveau 1808–1808 (died in infancy)
2 CONT Baby male Neveu 1809–1809 (died in infancy)
2 CONT Narcisse Neveu 1810–
2 CONT Marie-Julie Neveu 1811–
2 CONT Joseph-Norbert Neveau 1813–1814 (died in infancy)
2 CONT AURELIE NEVEU 1815–1897
2 CONT Sophie Neveau 1816–1816 (died in infancy)
2 CONT Julie Neveu 1817–1889
2 CONT Alexis Neveu 1819–1861
2 CONT Felix Neveu 1821–1894
2 CONT
2 CONT He died on 26 September 1822, in Saint-Cuthbert, Berthier, Quebec, Canada, at the age of 64, and was buried in Saint-Cuthbert, Berthier, Quebec, Canada.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
