1 NOTE {geni:about_me} A Patriot of the American Revolution for LOUISIANA.   [http://services.dar.org/Public/DAR_Research/search_adb/?action=full&p_id=A086239  DAR Ancestor # A086239]
2 CONT
2 CONT * Reference: [https://gw.geneanet.org/jeanmarcbouet?lang=en&p=charles&n=olivier+de+vezin Geneanet Genealogy] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Jan 24 2018, 15:59:08 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT ===Individual Note===
2 CONT Egalement donné comme étant né le 6 juin 1748 à Trois Rivières en Canada (Nouvelle France). Tableau : La Plantation Olivier de Vezin à Saint-Martinville par Adrien Persac* Reference: [https://gw.geneanet.org/jelumac?lang=en&iz=0&p
2 CONC =charles&n=olivier+de+vezin Geneanet Genealogy] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Aug 15 2018, 23:47:52 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.ancestry.com/family-tree/person/tree/1451775/person/6137127658 Ancestry Genealogy] - [https://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Nov 5 2018, 12:19:21 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT "Hughes Charles Honoré Dugué OLIVIER de Vézin de St-Maurice was born 8 June 1751 at Trois-Rivières, Québec to Louis Pierre François Marie OLIVIER de Vézin of France and Marie Joséphine GATINEAU du Plessis.  He was baptized 26 July
2 CONC  1751 in New Orleans. Baptismal sponsors were Honoré Michel DE LA ROUVILLIER – Royal Councilor and General Paymaster of the Navy in the Louisiana colony and Charlotte FLEURY, Marquise de Vaudreuil – épouse à Pierre RIGAUD, Marquis
2 CONC  de Vaudreuil – Governor of the Louisiana Province (SLC B22 226). He married c. 1770 Marie-Magdeleine DE MARIGNY DE MANDÉVILLE, daughter of Antoine Philippe DE MARIGNY DE MANDÉVILLE of France and Marie Françoise DUPART GASCHET de 
2 CONC l’Isle (NO Ch). By 1788, she [Marie-Magdeleine] had died, and Charles OLIVIER de Vézin had taken up with one mulâtresse mistress and soon would have an additional one. Adélaïde DUBREUIL – mulâtresse affranchie, daughter of Alexand
2 CONC re DUBREUIL and Marianne – négresse esclave. Magdeleine LACOSTE – mulâtresse libre, daughter of Jean LACOSTE and unknown négresse mother. He, along with both of his mulâtresse mistresses, arrived and settled in the Attakapas Distr
2 CONC ict between present-day Jeanerette and New Iberia along Bayou Têche. They formed the nucleus of the Free People of Color community of New Iberia/Grand-Marais with nearly 20 children total. Charles died on 24 April 1815 at his home
2 CONC  and was buried at his home on the east side of Bayou Teche below New Iberia, Iberia Parish, Louisiana.
2 CONT * Reference: [https://www.wikitree.com/wiki/Olivier-826 WikiTree Genealogy] - [http://www.geni.com/projects/SmartCopy/18783 SmartCopy]: ''Nov 5 2018, 23:04:40 UTC''
2 CONT
2 CONT ----
