1 NOTE {geni:about_me} '''Hermanus Bosman''' * Amsterdam 19.4.1682 s.v. Lambertus Bosman v. Aurik in Oos-Friesland wat op 6.9.1681 getroud is met Maria Fransz v. Amsterdam. Hermanus gaan in 1705 na Batavia as sieketrooster, maar in 1707 
2 CONC a. aan die Kaap op die Overryp. Hier word hy aangestel as sieketrooster en voorleser vir die gemeente Drakenstein. Hy tree in 1748 uit VOC-diens en woon op “De oude Plantage” † 26.7.1769 (sien verder Die Bosmans in Suid-Afrika deu
2 CONC r Sita de Kock) x 4.3.1708 Elisabeth DE VILLIERS * c. 1690 † c. 1765 d.v. Abraham de Villiers en Susanna Gardiol
2 CONT
2 CONT '''b2 Susanna''' ≈ 17.1.1712 x 3.8.1732 Izak DE VRIES
2 CONT
2 CONT Dogter van Hermanus Bosman. Sy was 'n skryfster.
2 CONT
2 CONT -=-=
2 CONT
2 CONT Susanna Bosman , the daughter of Abraham Bosman and Susanna de Villiers. She was born in 1712 at the Cape and died 9th July 1755.
2 CONT
2 CONT They lived in a house on Zee Street, Cape Town.
2 CONT
2 CONT They had four daughters and four sons.
2 CONT
2 CONT -=-=-=-
2 CONT
2 CONT Her children are given as listed in her will made in May, 1746,
2 CONT
2 CONT when, recently widowed, she was confined to bed by sickness.
2 CONT
2 CONT In this same will she appoints her brother-in-law, Daniel de Vries,
2 CONT
2 CONT to run the bakery for the benefit of her children if the Executors
2 CONT
2 CONT should see fit.
2 CONT
2 CONT In her will of 1755 she mentioned only her two youngest children,
2 CONT
2 CONT Hendrik and Elisabeth, mentioning that they should not go to live
2 CONT
2 CONT with anyone other their own family.
2 CONT
2 CONT In his will of 1785 her brother, Abraham Bosman, left a portion of
2 CONT
2 CONT his estate to be divided among the children of Susanna and Isaak
2 CONT
2 CONT but their two sons, Abraham and Hendrik, are excluded 'for
2 CONT
2 CONT special reasons
2 CONT
2 CONT -=-=-=-=-=-
2 CONT
