1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Jan de Villiers farmed Zorgvliet in Banhoek near Stellenbosch.
2 CONT
2 CONT Married to Anna de Villiers, 27 January 1771 in Paarl
2 CONT
2 CONT Son Jan Daniel de Villiers born 18 July 1779 in Stellenbosch
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Married to Anna de Villiers, 27 January 1771 in Paarl
2 CONT
2 CONT Son Jan Daniel de Villiers born 18 July 1779 in Stellenbosch
2 CONT
2 CONT Jan de Villiers 1745 was the Great Grandson of Jean de Villiers 1630 and Isabeau Sicaulttn 1637. He married Anna de Villiers 1754 who was the GGranddaughter of Jean de Villiers 1630 and Isabeau Sicaulttn 1637. (kissing cousins)
2 CONT
2 CONT Jan was born at Drakenstein on 24 Oct 1745 and he died at Stellenbosch on 22 Feb 1788. He farmed Zorgvliet  in Banhoek near Stellenbosch. On 27 Jan 1771 (when Captain Cook was discovering Australia) he married Anna de Villiers at 
2 CONC Paarl. She was the daughter of Jan de Villiers (don’t ask me) and Anna Hugo. She had been born on 17 Nov  1754. When her husband Jan died, she married the next year to Petrus Francois Rousseau, and took with her into that marriage
2 CONC  her 9 children of whom the 5th was Jan Daniel de Villiers.
2 CONT
