1 NOTE {geni:about_me} June 18m 1782.  Antoine Dequindre was born in Detroit.  Antoine served as a apprentice, clerk and in 1810 opened a store in the city.   During the War of 1812 he served as a Captain in the Michigan Legion at the Ba
2 CONC ttle of Monguason/Maguaga.   Antoines company was the first to attack and enter the British breastworks and later his men sank a British gunboat on the Rouge River from a cannon on shore.  The area is today's City of Riverview. De
2 CONC quindre Road that runs through Detroit, Oakland & Macomb counties was named after him.  He and his wife are interred in St. Anne's mass grave at Mt. Elliott Cemetery.  Credit City of Detroit 1710-1922, Volume 4/Detroit Historical 
2 CONC Society
