1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://dahlheimer-bebeau.com/Bebeau/RM-JacquesBibeau-Descendants/b4112.htm#P4112
2 CONT
2 CONT Hypolite (Paul) BIBEAU was born on 3 Sep 1796 in St Pierre-de-Sorel, Richelieu, Quebec, Canada.  He was baptized on 4 Sep 1796 in Sorel, Quebec, Canada.  He immigrated on 29 Aug 1847 to Detroit, Michigan, USA.  According to his De
2 CONC claration of Intention which was filed 3 July 1848, Paul Bibeau (Bebaux) arrived in the U.S. on 29 August 1847 at Detroit.
2 CONT
2 CONT His declaration date was 29 November 1847 before H. Jackson, j.p., Wisconsin Territory.
2 CONT
2 CONT By this declaration we know that Paul and his family arrived in MN sometime between 29 August 1847 and 3 July 1848.  He immigrated on 3 Jul 1848 to Little Canada, Ramsey, Minnesota, USA.  According to his Declaration of Intention 
2 CONC which was filed 3 July 1848, Paul Bibeau (Bebaux) arrived in the U.S. on 29 August 1847 at Detroit.
2 CONT
2 CONT His declaration date was 29 November 1847 before H. Jackson, j.p., Wisconsin Territory.
2 CONT
2 CONT By this declaration we know that Paul and his family arrived in MN sometime between 29 August 1847 and 3 July 1848. He died in 1866 in Little Canada, Ramsey, Minnesota, USA.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hypolite (Paul) BIBEAU and Veronique Catherine HUS DIT MILLET were married on 21 Sep 1824 in St Pierre-de-Sorel, Richelieu, Quebec, Canada. They appeared in the census in 1850 in Little Canada, Ramsey, Minnesota, USA.13 Census don
2 CONC e 15 Sep 1850
2 CONT
2 CONT Listed under Bibot: (all listed as born in Canada)
2 CONT
2 CONT Paul Bibot, 58, male, farmer Varounette, 45, female, Pierre, 22, male Xavier, 14, male Marie, 12, female Charles, 9, male David, 8, male Christine, 6, female Prudence, 4, female They appeared in the census in 1860 in White Bear La
2 CONC ke Township, Ramsey, Minnesota, USA. 1860 census, White Bear Lake, Ramsey, MN, p. 286 Conducted on 12 July 1860 Entries under the name: De Bane All born in Canada
2 CONT
2 CONT Paul, 66, m, farmer value of real estate $750 value of personal property $500
2 CONT
2 CONT Virginia, 55, f (=Veronique)
2 CONT
2 CONT (Not listed: - Catherine, married so would not be listed with parents - Other children who died before 1860: Alexis, Pierre, two infants, Marie Desanges - Desanges, married before 1860 so not listed with parents - Pelagie, not sur
2 CONC e if she was alive at this time - Francois-Xavier, died before 1860 - Marie, married before 1860 - Christine, died before 1860
2 CONT
2 CONT Charles, 20, m, farm labourer David, 16, m, farm labourer Christine, 14, f Prudence, 13, f
2 CONT
2 CONT And listed in household: Chas. Carrol 25, m, farm laborer Veronique Catherine HUS DIT MILLET was born on 5 Oct 1807 in St Pierre-de-Sorel, Richelieu, Quebec, Canada. She died on 28 Jan 1865 in Little Canada, Ramsey, Minnesota, USA
