1 NOTE 1860 fed. census: Willsboro, Essex, NY; p.399; Pascal St. George
2 CONT
2 CONT 1850 fed. census; Willsboro, Essex, NY; "Pascall St. George"; 25 y.o. collier; with wife Caroline and Adeline (68 y.o.); married within the last  year (this Pascal is prob. the son of Louis & Julia St. George who live next door)
2 CONT
2 CONT moved from NY to WI about 1855 (with Terrio family)
2 CONT
2 CONT 1860 fed. census; Ripon twp., Fond du Lac, WI; "Paschal St. George"; 32 y.o. farmer; living next to his sister and her husband, John Terrio
2 CONT
2 CONT 1870 fed. census; Brooklyn twp. (Ripon P.O.), Green Lake, WI; "Paschall St. George"; 40 y.o. farmer (no wife)
2 CONT
2 CONT 1880 fed. census: Little Wolf twp., Waupaca, WI; 126C; Pascal St. George, 54 y.o. born in Canada; living with second wife, Mary Ann
2 CONT
2 CONT 1900 fed. census; Little Wolf twp., Waupaca, WI; 76 y.o. widower "Paskel St. George" with daughter Caroline
2 CONT
2 CONT 1910 fed. census; Little Wolf twp., Waupaca, WI; ED 82; p.202 (11A); "Pascal St. George"; 85 y.o.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT See "Gazette, Stevens Point, WI" 16 Nov 1921
2 CONT
2 CONT Thanks for writing and I apologize for taking so long to respond.
2 CONT I don't think I have anything that will help you. I just started working on my John Terrio - Angeline St. George lines. I do not have any information relating John Terrio's parents, grandparents, etc.
2 CONT Angeline St. George had a brother Paschal St. George who lived in Manawa. He and Angeline were the children of one Pascal St. George. I do not know who their mother was. I have sent for a copy of Angeline's obituary and hope it wi
2 CONC ll be of some help identifying her parents.
2 CONT Paschal St. George died in Manawa in September 1921. The article published in the Manawa Advocate relating to his death states that he is survived by one brother, Alfred St. George, of Iowa and two sisters, Mrs. Angeline Terrio of
2 CONC  Waupaca and Mrs. Adolph Glodgo of Wausau.
2 CONT Paschal is buried in the Sacred Heart Cemetery at Manawa, WI. The following information was sent to me and was taken from various gravemarkers in the family plot:
2 CONT St. George, Grandma (nothing else, believed to Paschal wife )
2 CONT " " , Paschal, 1824-1921
2 CONT " " , Caroline A. dau of P.& C., 1855-1933
2 CONT " " , Rose, Wife of Fred, 1859-1936
2 CONT " " , Fred, 1857-1939
2 CONT " " , Charles H., son of F. & R. 1882-1933
2 CONT " " , Elizabeth Jean, dau. of M. & A., 1925-1945
2 CONT Sorry I couldn't be of more help. I'll keep your address and if I come across anything I'll send it on to you.
