2 CONT <p>Named in a congressional report as part of the Pembina Band. 1871 investigation referring back to the&nbsp;Treaty of 1863 held at the Red River Crossing which was the Sixth Session of land in Minnesota by the Ojibwe. In 1873, h
2 CONC e was allotted a portion of the White Earth Reserve by an act of Congress.</p>
