1 NOTE {geni:about_me} On December 24, 1812 she bought stands 185, 60, 66 and 54 (currently no. 36) from JD Mohr for 3000 guilders. The latter had bought the land from J.D.Maree, which in turn in 1796 the church obtained. The fancy-store
2 CONC y house (famous De Wet House) was built by the traditional Thibault design. The architects who in 1969 restored after the earthquake, however, could not find evidence for this assumption to have occurred. Travelers Burchell at his
2 CONC  arrival in Shimla took awhile to be impressed by this favorable, friendly and pleasant place.   As a widow her rights and status stood. With the death of her husband she had to surrender her correct place in the front row of the 
2 CONC church which she refused to do. The consistory was in a predicament and thought of the  pulpit having to be moved backwards.  After discussion it was decided to move   the chairs closer together in order to put an extra row of cha
2 CONC irs to solve the problem. On another occasion, the irrigation water for her garden was starting to flow too slowly to properly water her garden. At her insistence to do the investigating she found dirt. The other stand owners were
2 CONC  required to send their slaves to clean the ditch for her. On May 31, 1822 her house was sold at a public auction to PF Theron for 25,000 guilders. She then moved to Worcester
2 CONT  In 1848, with the appointment of the first resident-magistrate of Shimla, the Member  Wet-House rentals as magistrates and was then known as heemradehuis. The house then changed owners  several times. In November 1949 Sir Alfred 
2 CONC Beit got it and he then restored the house with an architect. Hildegard Erika, wife of Dr. Helmut Silberberg, bought the house in 1964 and named it  'Mon Bijou "(My Old).
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT Catharina Maria Hugo - a1b3c4d4 - het in 1812 die bekende De Wet huis  in Tulbach laat bou wat deur Thibault ontwerp is.
2 CONT
2 CONT Bron:
2 CONT
2 CONT Geslagregister van ou Kaapse families - Christoffel Coetzee de Villiers
