1 OCCU Farmer. Vineyard owner.
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Jan Daniel de Villiers owned and farmed  Zorgvliet at Banhoek near Stellenbosch. He had inherited the property from his mother.
2 CONT
2 CONT Married to Cecilia Maria van der Merwe, 3 August 1800 in Cape Town
2 CONT
2 CONT Cecilia Maria van der Merwe died 18 April 1813 in Paarl
2 CONT
2 CONT Married to Johanna Margaretha de Villiers, 2 October 1813 in Paarl
2 CONT
2 CONT Anna Cornelia Albertina de Villiers born 1 January 1816 in Cape Town, South Africa.
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Jan Daniel de Villiers owned and farmed  Zorgvliet at Banhoek near Stellenbosch. He had inherited the property from his mother.
2 CONT
2 CONT Jan Daniel was born at Banhoek and was Christened at Stellenbosch on 18 Jul 1779. He died at Groot-Drakenstein on 22 Nov 1836. He was a wine farmer on Zorgvliet at Banhoek, which he had inherited from his mother. He married Cecili
2 CONC a Maria van der Merwe in Cape Town on 03 Aug 1800. She was the daughter of Jacob van der Merwe and Cecilia Maria van Herden and had been born on 26 Aug 1781. After her fourth child, she died at Paarl on 18 Apr 1813. Six months lat
2 CONC er Jan Daniel de Villiers then married  Johanna Margaretha de Villiers at Paarl on 02 Oct 1813. She had been baptised on 26 Jan 1777 the daughter of Petrus Johannes de Villiers and Susanna Maria de Villiers. She was the widow of J
2 CONC acobus Philippus Louw. Jan Daniel de Villiers and Johanna Margaretha de Villiers had one child, a daughter. She was named Anna Cornelia Albertina de Villiers.
