2 CONT ---------
2 CONT
2 CONT By 1784 Paul Roux Snr had acquired at least half of the original Fleurbaai land, as it had been depicted in 1736.
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1806 '''Jacobus Roux''' (at other times referred to as Paul Jacobus), '''snr''', gifted the farm Fleurbaai 
2 CONT (cited as part of Vredenberg) to his son, Paul, at no cost to him or to his son, confirmed by the fiscal at the Castle of Good Hope. This was implemented in Deed in 1842 (being 33 morgen 454.5sqr freehold of the place Fleurbaai) a
2 CONC long with the transfer of quitrent land adjacent. 
2 CONT
2 CONT During the early part of the 19th century Paul Roux, snr acquired numerous pieces of quitrent land adjacent, and by the time transfer of the land took place, he owned Vredenberg, Vlottenburg, Fleurbaai and his brother, '''JP Roux'
2 CONC '' owned Libertas. 
2 CONT
2 CONT In 1813 Paul Roux requested a piece of Quitrent land, which was surveyed in 1814 and granted in 1818. Paul Roux Jacobus’ son (i.e. Paul Roux junior) was granted 161 morgen, 484.5 sqr quitrent land adjacent to Fleurbaai9 on conditi
2 CONC on that public roads remain open. The land granted was located with the Helderberg to the South, contiguous with the property of P Roux Senior and wasteland to the west, and Libertas to the east. Two diagrams are used to depict th
2 CONC e land. The quitrent grant diagram was replaced in 1959. This is comparable with the east part of an 1883 surveyor’s diagram. 
2 CONT
2 CONT The 1814 diagram depicts a homestead (marked as such), flanked by a pair of outbuildings, immediately south of the land that had been transferred to Paul Roux in 1784 (the original grant), and for which he was now applying as he h
2 CONC ad been farming it. 
2 CONT In addition, in 1814 the land north of the Eersteriver was granted to Paul Roux Senior10. This grant 
2 CONT was described as 358 morgen 474 sqr, bounded to the north by the farm of widow Marais and the 
2 CONT outspan place near Stellenbosch town (‘dorp’), East to the farm of Jac’ (Jacobus) Roux, '''Jac’s''' son, south to the Eerste river and the farm of Roux, and west to the untamed veld and the farm of A van der Byl. Two portions were
2 CONC  divided off in 1824 and transferred to Paul Roux junior, and the remainder became Vlottenburg. The total landholding was in excess of 519 morgen, or approximately 445 hectares (over a thousand acres).
2 CONT
2 CONT There are at least 4 generations of men all called Paul Roux and owners of this land, referred to in the Title 
2 CONT Deeds. The family links and details have not been researched, but the generations are referred to as senior, junior and grandson for the sake of the clarity of the document. Where a statement of inferred age related status is made
2 CONC , it is taken from the Deed. 
2 CONT
2 CONT 9 SQ 4.43, December 1818
2 CONT
2 CONT 10 SQ 4.3, 13 March 1818, surveyed 1814
2 CONT
2 CONT Reference: REMAINDER PORTION 6 OF THE FARM FLEURBAAI NUMBER 1040, STELLENBOSCH HERITAGE REPORT ACCOMPANYING ANNEXURE A:
2 CONT APPLICATION FOR A PERMIT UNDER SECTION 27 OF THE NATIONAL HERITAGE RESOURCES ACT OF 1999. PREPARED FOR WATERFALL TRUST BY MIKE SCURR OF RENNIE SCURR ADENDORFF ARCHITECTS cc
2 CONT AUGUST 2014
2 CONT
