1 NOTE {geni:about_me} "The remains of the late Denis J. Campau were buried yesterday in the family lot of the Campaus in Mount Elliott Cemetery.  The funeral services were held in St. Anne's Church, the spiritual home of the family of t
2 CONC he deceased for considerably more than half a century.  There was a large representation of old citizens in attendance of the solemn last rites, the church and casket were beautifully decorated with flowers, and the impressive ser
2 CONC vice for the dead of the Roman Catholic Church was conducted by Rev. Ernest Van Dyke assisted by Rev Anciaux, Pastor of St. Anne's, and vicor general Hennaert.  A detail of police bore the remains from the church to the hearse, th
2 CONC e attendant pall bearers being Alex Lewis, C. A. Kent, Col. Wm D. Wilkins, Theodore Romeyn, Col. Freeman Norvell, A. C. McGraw, E. V. Cicott, and Elisha Taylor.  The funeral cortege was very long and imposing, and the attendance o
2 CONC f the church was unusually large"     August 20, 1878   Detroit Free Press
