0 @N6000000000250401282@ NOTE De la Ronde and Thibaudiere. He was one of the voyagers who removed from Drummond Island to Penetanguishene when the garrison there was closed in 1828.  During his lifetime he was a resident of Penetanguishene, Holland Landing, an
1 CONC d Coldwater. He was a fur trader at Penetanguishene and suffered heavily when falsely imprisoned there by other merchants of Montreal. The Indians considered him as one who was dead and would therefore do no business with him.
1 CONT
1 CONT Source:
1 CONT
1 CONT The History of Denis de Laronde family, 15th to 20th century.  Compiled by E. Bacon Vaughan. (Windsor, 1949).
